From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:19:12 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] mics: present the processed microphone as MONO, not AUX0

Every microphone graph published its single processed channel as AUX0.
AUX0 has no place in a stereo layout, so a stereo client (GNOME
Settings, browsers, most recorders) got the microphone in the left
channel only and silence on the right.

Position the output channel as MONO. PipeWire then gives a stereo
client the microphone on both channels. The capture side keeps AUX0-2
for the raw mics, which is what 43f4ff8 changed to stop the third mic
being dropped as LFE.

On the J616s, a 2-channel recording from the processed source read
L -36.6 dBFS, R silent with AUX0, and L -32.3, R -32.3 dBFS with MONO.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
[J604 recipe: the firs/j616/mic.json hunk dropped; that file is not in the pinned 06aec67a]
